From ce1a4ea6aac4c6d5c26aa8f9da61a2dfc44b0fdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: salvia420-bit <salvia420@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:43:26 -0330
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Vehicles (holtburger fork): server-authoritative Hellcat
 demo, HBV1 protocol, fast-flight streaming

Server side of the holtburger vehicles design (holtburger
apps/holtburger-web/docs/vehicles-2026-11-01: DESIGN.md + decisions log,
HANDOFF.md). Every feature sits behind a server property that defaults off;
with all of them off ACE behaves as upstream.

- HBV1 wire messages in 0xF7B1 / 0xF7B0 (opcodes 0x0900-0x090F) with a
  capability handshake; non-capable clients see a retail stand-in object.
- VehicleManager: input-driven authoritative flight model (parity-tested
  against the client predictor), board / exit / bail-out with a
  server-simulated parachute fall, gun with server-side hit resolution,
  derelict crash and despawn, retail chat line, @vehicle / @vehicles.
- Streaming for 400 km/h: corridor preload on background tasks (world thread
  never waits on them), per-pilot 350 m tiered sight, 60 s retention,
  spawn-cache and indoor-cell warm-ups, a per-tick budget for landblocks
  only vehicles have visited (loot generation waits for a player on foot).
- Diagnostics: WorldTickMonitor and [VEHICLE][...] log lines.
- Tests: ACE.Server.Tests/Vehicles (wire fixtures, flight parity, input
  queue, spread RNG, HouseCell warm-up).

Properties: vehicles_enabled, landblock_wake_on_entry, vehicle_preload,
vehicle_preload_offthread, vehicle_short_retention, vehicle_landblock_budget,
vehicle_retail_chat, vehicle_speed_cap, vehicle_sight_radius.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
